  "outline": [
    "Rebuilt 26 Oct 2026 on Adrian's first notes: the diagram on the board straight away; no opening (no question read, no corner plan) before 'what it says'; the dot ANIMATED O → A → O → B → O while the graph of x against t draws out (the swing figure), then a and n read off the graph.",
    "What it says: the screen picture (A, O, B, 120 cm, 60 each side), x = a sin nt with each letter lit and its meaning written.",
    "One oscillation (A's side positive): the swing plays — the dot goes O, A, O, B, O while the sine curve is drawn at its height; A is the top of the graph, B the bottom.",
    "(a) from the graph: the highest point = the furthest from O = 60; sin nt is between −1 and 1 so x is between −a and a: the highest point is a, so a = 120/2 = 60. One full wave = one oscillation = 6 s; for sin nt one wave takes 2π/n (why: a drop-down), so 2π/n = 6 ⇒ n = π/3; x = 60 sin(πt/3).",
    "(b) v = dx/dt = 60 cos(πt/3) × π/3 = 20π cos(πt/3); |cos| ≤ 1 so max speed = 20π cm/s.",
    "(c) d²x/dt² = −(20π²/3) sin(πt/3); at A (the top of the graph) x = 60, so sin(πt/3) = 1 — no t needed (t = 1.5 is when it first gets there: a drop-down); acceleration −(20π²/3)(1), magnitude 20π²/3 = 65.8 cm/s² (3 s.f.)."
  ],
